{"name":"Butter White","hex":"#fddebd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"butter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soft, fatty foodstuff made by churning the cream of milk (generally cow's milk).","Any of various foodstuffs made from other foods or oils, similar in consistency to, eaten like or intended as a substitute for butter (preceded by the name of the food used to make it)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spread butter on.","To move one's weight backwards or forwards onto the tips or tails of one's skis or snowboard so only the tip or tail is in contact with the snow. Similar to applying butter to bread with the end of a knife.\nTo spin on skis or a snowboard using only the tips or tails being in contact with the snow"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butter"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Butter","blocks":[{"text":"Butter is a dairy product made from the fat and protein components of churned cream. It is a semi-solid emulsion at room temperature, consisting of approximately 81% butterfat. It is used at room temperature as a spread, melted as a condiment, and used as a fat in baking, sauce-making, pan frying, and other cooking procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butter","wikidata":"Q34172"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/500px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/1280px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Buttered_crumpet3.jpg/500px-Buttered_crumpet3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Butter spread on a crumpet using a butter knife","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AButtered_crumpet3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Churning_butter.jpg/500px-Churning_butter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Churning_butter.jpg/1280px-Churning_butter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Churning_butter.jpg/500px-Churning_butter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th